"For thousands of years, people in Africa, the Middle East and South Asia have cleaned their teeth with chewing sticks called miswak. Chewing makes more spit, which protects teeth. From 1901 to 1945, three scientists solved the “Colorado Stain” mystery. Too much fluoride in drinking water stained teeth. But a tiny amount meant far fewer cavities. Later, scientists learned why: fluoride helps enamel rebuild stronger.":"几千年来，非洲、中东和南亚的人们一直用叫作 Miswak 的咀嚼棒清洁牙齿。咀嚼能产生更多口水来保护牙齿。1901 到 1945 年间，三位科学家解开了“科罗拉多牙斑”之谜：饮用水里氟化物太多会让牙齿变色，但只要有一点点，蛀牙就会少得多。后来科学家明白了原因：氟化物能帮牙釉质重建得更坚固。",
