"In 1–2 days, germs left alone build sticky slime domes that rinses can’t wash off. Brushing and flossing break them. That matters in space, where there is no dentist nearby!":"只要 1–2 天不管，细菌就会搭起漱口水冲不掉的黏液罩。刷牙和用牙线能打破它们。这在太空里特别重要，因为附近可没有牙医！",
"In 1498 in China, people set stiff hog hairs into a bone handle. It was the first bristle toothbrush. In 1683 in Delft, Antonie van Leeuwenhoek looked at plaque from his own teeth with a microscope he made. He saw millions of tiny swimming germs. Vinegar could not kill the germs hiding deep in thick plaque!":"1498 年在中国，人们把硬猪鬃装进骨头手柄里，做出了第一把鬃毛牙刷。1683 年在代尔夫特，Antonie van Leeuwenhoek 用自己做的显微镜观察自己牙齿上的牙菌斑，看到了数百万游动的微小细菌。食醋可杀不死藏在厚厚牙菌斑深处的细菌！",
"In 1819 in New Orleans, dentist Levi Spear Parmly told people to use waxed silk floss to clean between teeth, where no brush fits. More than 100 years later in the same city, Dr. Charles Bass studied the tiny gap where gums meet teeth. He taught the gentle 45° soft-brush method used all over the world today.":"1819 年在新奥尔良，牙医 Levi Spear Parmly 建议人们用涂蜡丝质牙线清洁牙刷伸不进的牙缝。100 多年后在同一座城市，Charles Bass 医生研究了牙龈和牙齿交界处的细小缝隙，教大家使用如今传遍全世界的 45° 轻柔软毛刷牙法。",
"In 1940 in Chicago, Dr. Robert Stephan put tiny sensors right on people’s plaque. Within 3 minutes of a sugar rinse, the plaque turned acid enough to harm enamel. It took 20 to 40 minutes for spit to wash the acid away.":"1940 年在芝加哥，Robert Stephan 医生把微型传感器直接放在人们的牙菌斑上。用糖水漱口不到 3 分钟，牙菌斑变酸的程度就足以伤害牙釉质。口水要花 20 到 40 分钟才能把酸冲走。",
"In space there is no sink to spit in. A sticky germ slime dome is trying to take over the molars.":"太空里没有吐口水的水池。黏糊糊的细菌黏液罩正想占领磨牙。",
"In space, slime domes block the brush! Cut them open with Floss or blast them with Surge, then sweep clean.":"在太空里，黏液罩会挡住牙刷！用牙线切开它们，或者用爆发轰开它们，再刷干净。",
